---
import Journey from '../../layouts/Journey.astro';
import Step from '../../components/journey/Step.astro';
import Next from '../../components/journey/Next.astro';
import More from '../../components/journey/More.astro';
import Fact from '../../components/data/Fact.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/nav';
---
<Journey chapter="parallel" first="three" title="Side by side" description="Several agents can work at once if each has its own copy of the project. Their finished work is merged into the main branch one piece at a time.">
  <Step id="three" title="Three at once, one folder">
    <p><a href={url('journey/handoff/')}>The helper from step 6</a>, three of them at once, all in one folder. In this made-up run they overwrite each other’s files.</p>
  </Step>
  <Step id="copies" title="Give each its own copy">
    <p>Each helper now stands on its own copy of the project. Finished work is merged into main one piece at a time.</p>
    <div class="pick">
      <button type="button" data-do="own" data-val="own" data-default aria-pressed="true">A copy each</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="own" data-val="shared" aria-pressed="false">One shared folder</button>
    </div>
    <More title="The commands">
      <p>Git calls such a copy a worktree. For a made-up task called search:</p>
      <pre class="j-code"><code>{`git worktree add ../club-search -b search
# the helper works in ../club-search
git merge search
git worktree remove ../club-search`}</code></pre>
      <p><Fact id="harnesses.claudeCode.subagentWorktree" show="claim" /></p>
    </More>
  </Step>
  <Step id="more" title="How many?">
    <p>More helpers finish more tasks. Main still takes one merge at a time, and every report lands in the agent’s window.</p>
    <div class="controls">
      <label class="control"><span>Helpers <output>5</output></span>
        <input type="range" min="1" max="5" step="1" value="5" data-bind="n" />
      </label>
    </div>
    <Next from="parallel" more={[{ href: 'explain/orchestration/', text: 'Ways to split work' }]} />
  </Step>
</Journey>
